Package: inlavanilla
Title: INLA-Style Skew-Normal Marginals for Any Log-Posterior
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Haziq", "Jamil", , "haziq.jamil@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3298-1010")),
    person("Håvard", "Rue", role = "ctb",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0222-1881", "Statistical and computational methodology")),
    person("Thomas", "Luu", role = "cph",
           comment = "Skew-normal quantile approximation (Apache License 2.0)")
  )
Description: Performs approximate Bayesian inference for the parameters of a
    model from its log-likelihood plus log-prior alone, using the
    approximation pipeline of the 'INLAvaan' package (Jamil & Rue, 2026a)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2603.25690>, an adaptation of the Integrated
    Nested Laplace Approximation (Rue et al., 2009)
    <doi:10.1111/j.1467-9868.2008.00700.x>, with no latent field and nothing
    model-specific. A Laplace approximation with a variational Bayes mean
    correction gives the log marginal likelihood, a skew-normal is fitted to
    each parameter's marginal by scanning the log-posterior, and a Gaussian
    copula couples the marginals for posterior draws. See also Jamil and Rue
    (2026b) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2604.00671>. Leave-one-out cross-validation
    and the widely applicable information criterion come from a second-order
    Taylor expansion of the pointwise log-likelihood (Alhyari et al., 2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2609.00670>.
